WEBVTT

1
00:02:41.168 --> 00:02:45.667
Victory over France!
Victory over France!

2
00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:49.210
Western Front surrenders!

3
00:03:06.668 --> 00:03:08.502
Good morning, Judge Fromm.

4
00:03:09.502 --> 00:03:13.501
- There's nothing for you today.
- That is what I call good news.

5
00:03:13.502 --> 00:03:15.876
I wish you a nice day just the same.

6
00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:17.752
Your Honour.

7
00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:30.126
- Heil Hitler!
- Heil Hitler!

8
00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:31.626
So what's the news?

9
00:03:31.627 --> 00:03:35.251
A letter from the military postal service.
Typed.

10
00:03:35.252 --> 00:03:36.543
Who?

11
00:03:38.085 --> 00:03:40.668
Quangels' son.

12
00:04:03.502 --> 00:04:05.585
Herr Quangel. For you.

13
00:04:59.168 --> 00:05:01.418
Something has happened to the boy?

14
00:05:08.543 --> 00:05:11.043
Those liars!

15
00:05:16.168 --> 00:05:17.834
Anna.

16
00:05:17.835 --> 00:05:22.127
You're to blame. You and your damn war!
You and your damn Fuhrer!

17
00:05:37.752 --> 00:05:41.960
- Anna...
- Please. Leave me alone.

18
00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:42.320
FarangSiam thanks you.
Have Fun!

19
00:06:53.168 --> 00:06:55.252
It's me, Eva.

20
00:06:55.418 --> 00:06:57.293
Frau Rosenthal?

21
00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.460
Anything from my husband?

22
00:07:13.918 --> 00:07:16.251
- Thank you, Eva.
- What do you need?

23
00:07:16.252 --> 00:07:20.293
I don't need much.
As always.

24
00:07:29.127 --> 00:07:35.668
ALONE IN BERLIN

25
00:08:14.668 --> 00:08:17.668
ARMISTICE SIGNED IN COMPIEGNE

26
00:09:10.418 --> 00:09:14.043
YOU TOO

27
00:09:28.002 --> 00:09:30.168
Frau Quangel.
How much butter do you need?

28
00:09:31.168 --> 00:09:33.293
Half a pound? Your usual?

29
00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.710
You have milk and eggs.
Now, how much butter do you need?

30
00:09:39.918 --> 00:09:43.043
- Oh, come on!
- Hurry up. Come along.

31
00:09:49.252 --> 00:09:52.668
Frau Quangel?
I'll take you home.

32
00:10:31.793 --> 00:10:35.418
HANS QUANGEL
23 JANUARY 1940

33
00:11:36.585 --> 00:11:39.710
THE LIAR

34
00:12:10.627 --> 00:12:13.377
I'll be straight home from work.

35
00:12:17.752 --> 00:12:22.252
Hey, Quangel. What's the hurry?
Is something wrong?

36
00:12:23.543 --> 00:12:27.377
We're going to get rich.
A victory over France.

37
00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:32.043
Know what that means? We're going to be
the richest country in the whole world!

38
00:12:40.293 --> 00:12:44.627
So, in the next few weeks we will have
destroyed England and ended the war.

39
00:12:45.043 --> 00:12:49.292
And since the troops on the front
have been so victorious,

40
00:12:49.293 --> 00:12:53.834
it's time that those of us at home
do our duty as well.

41
00:12:53.835 --> 00:12:56.501
The Fuhrer wants to increase production.

42
00:12:56.502 --> 00:13:00.459
He expects productivity to rise
by thirty percent in three months

43
00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.959
...and to double that within the next half a year.

44
00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.502
The Fuhrer's wish is our command.

45
00:13:07.918 --> 00:13:11.376
We will now receive any proposals
about how to reach this goal.

46
00:13:11.377 --> 00:13:13.377
- Sieg Heil!
- Sieg Heil!

47
00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.960
Workers, does anyone have anything to say?

48
00:13:21.377 --> 00:13:23.627
Yes, Foreman Quangel?

49
00:13:24.502 --> 00:13:29.542
To increase productivity, additional
machines must be installed

50
00:13:29.543 --> 00:13:32.126
...and a few shirkers laid off.

51
00:13:32.127 --> 00:13:35.626
What are you talking about?
Who are those shirkers?

52
00:13:35.627 --> 00:13:38.752
Some can't keep up with the work pace.
Others don't want to.

53
00:13:39.627 --> 00:13:45.751
Talking politics, skipping work. Some
men here are good at it. Very good.

54
00:13:45.752 --> 00:13:50.001
How dare you talk like that, Quangel!
You're not in the Party!

55
00:13:50.002 --> 00:13:52.167
How dare you discredit members of the Party!

56
00:13:52.168 --> 00:13:54.417
Quangel only thinks of himself.

57
00:13:54.418 --> 00:13:58.252
Do you donate anything to the Winter Relief Fund?
And to the Fuhrer?

58
00:14:00.293 --> 00:14:03.043
Germany has taken my only son.

59
00:14:04.127 --> 00:14:07.667
Yesterday, I was informed he died in combat.

60
00:14:07.668 --> 00:14:09.876
For you. For the Fuhrer.

61
00:14:09.877 --> 00:14:12.584
I ask you, Dolfuss:

62
00:14:12.585 --> 00:14:18.127
What more can a man donate...
than his child?

63
00:14:29.627 --> 00:14:32.959
Anna! Anna, we have visits to make!

64
00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.668
The Nazi Women's League is waiting for you!

65
00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:38.334
Heil Hitler, Anna!
Where were you?

66
00:14:38.335 --> 00:14:39.876
- We're late!
- Now, come on, it's time to go.

67
00:14:39.877 --> 00:14:42.002
- We'll wait downstairs.
- I'll change. I'll change.

68
00:14:45.585 --> 00:14:48.917
So, first that Frau Gerda Kleinschmidt.

69
00:14:48.918 --> 00:14:53.043
Then there's a Frau Else Wernicke
who just lives around the corner, then...

70
00:14:53.252 --> 00:14:55.501
listen to this: Claire Gehrich.

71
00:14:55.502 --> 00:14:57.626
She's the wife of Obersturmbannfuhrer Gehrich.

72
00:14:57.627 --> 00:15:00.042
You have to be really diplomatic if you visit her.

73
00:15:00.043 --> 00:15:01.792
- Should I cross her out?
- No, we can't do that.

74
00:15:01.793 --> 00:15:03.417
We all have to do our part.

75
00:15:03.418 --> 00:15:07.752
But... perhaps not today. We have to be
in good shape for someone like that.

76
00:15:27.752 --> 00:15:31.710
- What a nice place.
- What can I do for you?

77
00:15:32.418 --> 00:15:35.168
- Your husband?
- Yes.

78
00:15:36.043 --> 00:15:39.126
Your husband's fighting in Poland,
isn't he, Frau Kleinschmidt?

79
00:15:39.127 --> 00:15:42.459
He's risking his life, day after day,
for his people and his Fatherland

80
00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.376
while you are having a good time in Berlin.

81
00:15:45.377 --> 00:15:52.002
- Aren't you ashamed?
- But, I... but... nobody understands.

82
00:15:53.168 --> 00:15:55.293
I'm so worried for him.

83
00:15:56.002 --> 00:15:58.210
I'm so worried.

84
00:16:49.252 --> 00:16:50.460
Lock it off!

85
00:16:51.543 --> 00:16:53.293
Get back to work.

86
00:17:02.127 --> 00:17:05.043
Don't think this will save you
from the front I'm not going to lie.

87
00:17:05.585 --> 00:17:10.127
I know you did it on purpose.

88
00:17:11.502 --> 00:17:13.543
You understand?

89
00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.543
If the doorbell rings,
don't open the door. For anyone.

90
00:18:54.918 --> 00:18:57.210
- Otto?
- I'm writing.

91
00:19:00.543 --> 00:19:04.668
- To who?
- I don't know...

92
00:19:06.543 --> 00:19:08.627
I'm writing cards.

93
00:19:09.543 --> 00:19:12.127
Cards that tell the truth.

94
00:19:16.543 --> 00:19:19.002
People will read these cards.

95
00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.918
They will pass them on.

96
00:19:29.752 --> 00:19:35.001
Cards? You're scribbling cards?

97
00:19:35.002 --> 00:19:37.043
What is that supposed to do?

98
00:19:42.252 --> 00:19:46.043
MOTHER, THE FUHRER MURDERED MY SON...

99
00:19:46.877 --> 00:19:49.752
HE WILL MURDER YOUR SON TOO.
PASS THIS CARD ON.

100
00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:04.668
- Why are you writing like that?
- I'm disguising my handwriting.

101
00:20:07.668 --> 00:20:10.085
Let me do it. Please.

102
00:20:33.418 --> 00:20:35.377
It isn't even locked.

103
00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.668
- What if she screams?
- She won't scream.

104
00:20:41.877 --> 00:20:44.084
My stupid wife takes food to her.

105
00:20:44.085 --> 00:20:46.002
The old Jew...

106
00:20:46.877 --> 00:20:50.877
she hauled all her stuff up here
after they burned her shop.

107
00:20:53.043 --> 00:20:55.418
She's hiding.

108
00:21:13.252 --> 00:21:15.502
Psst! Calm down!

109
00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.793
- Papa, upstairs.
- Let's go. Quickly.

110
00:21:38.877 --> 00:21:41.252
What are you doing here?

111
00:21:42.252 --> 00:21:45.210
Barkhausen, what are you doing in this apartment?

112
00:21:46.002 --> 00:21:47.335
Herr Persicke...

113
00:21:48.293 --> 00:21:50.210
Neighbour, we can share.

114
00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.793
It's Frau Rosenthal.

115
00:22:15.043 --> 00:22:17.168
- Please, it's not my fault.
- Out.

116
00:22:19.543 --> 00:22:21.085
Look for the money.

117
00:22:29.585 --> 00:22:34.085
- I'm sorry.
- There is no need to be.

118
00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.877
- You can stay with us.
- This is too dangerous for you.

119
00:23:39.585 --> 00:23:42.251
- Judge Fromm?
- Come with me, Madame.

120
00:23:42.252 --> 00:23:45.210
Quickly. They'll be back.

121
00:23:50.002 --> 00:23:52.668
Be quiet. Come in.

122
00:24:10.918 --> 00:24:13.084
My deceased daughter's room.

123
00:24:13.085 --> 00:24:16.918
No one will look for you here.
Try to get used to it.

124
00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:22.377
Go to sleep and tomorrow morning
you will listen exactly to what I say.

125
00:24:22.835 --> 00:24:24.627
Tomorrow.
Good night, Frau Rosenthal.

126
00:25:05.127 --> 00:25:07.543
Is she back in her apartment?

127
00:25:30.043 --> 00:25:34.167
- No.
- I'm coming with you. You can't stop me.

128
00:25:34.168 --> 00:25:35.584
You can't stop me.

129
00:25:35.585 --> 00:25:37.667
They'll hang you.
They hang women, too.

130
00:25:37.668 --> 00:25:39.585
Of course they do.

131
00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:50.627
You only go up to the building.
I go inside. I place the card.

132
00:26:47.793 --> 00:26:49.335
I'll be right back.

133
00:28:00.502 --> 00:28:04.002
I'll be with you in a minute.
This way, sir.

134
00:28:05.002 --> 00:28:06.293
Eighty pfennig, please.

135
00:29:05.002 --> 00:29:07.792
- A schnapps.
- Coffee for me.

136
00:29:07.793 --> 00:29:10.085
No, I'll have a schnapps, too.

137
00:29:15.877 --> 00:29:17.627
So, we begin.

138
00:29:23.627 --> 00:29:25.793
From now on we are alone.

139
00:29:34.377 --> 00:29:36.459
You will not leave this room.

140
00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:40.918
For a certain period of time...
possibly a long time, you are my guest.

141
00:29:41.543 --> 00:29:46.084
But believe me, the moment you step out of that door...

142
00:29:46.085 --> 00:29:47.918
I will no longer know you.

143
00:29:48.793 --> 00:29:52.209
You know what they called me
in the courtroom, don't you?

144
00:29:52.210 --> 00:29:55.585
No? Cold-blooded Fromm.

145
00:29:56.627 --> 00:30:00.085
I have a mistress whom I obey.

146
00:30:01.377 --> 00:30:03.627
Her name is Justice.

147
00:30:06.085 --> 00:30:12.668
But I want to be in the apartment
when my husband arrives.

148
00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:17.168
He isn't coming back, and you know that, Frau Rosenthal.

149
00:30:18.627 --> 00:30:20.627
Lock the door. Yes?

150
00:30:29.835 --> 00:30:31.959
Where is this Barkhausen, then?
Where does he live?

151
00:30:31.960 --> 00:30:32.960
It's right here.

152
00:30:33.918 --> 00:30:36.834
Have you heard of that old woman that disappeared?

153
00:30:36.835 --> 00:30:38.459
I know her.

154
00:30:38.460 --> 00:30:41.168
See what they want. Go on!

155
00:30:46.168 --> 00:30:49.251
- Is the old man at home?
- What's it got to do with you?

156
00:30:49.252 --> 00:30:50.959
A lot.

157
00:30:50.960 --> 00:30:54.335
It's got a lot to do with the police, too,
and with the man at the Party.

158
00:30:56.418 --> 00:30:59.626
That's him, Inspector.
It was him and the other bum,

159
00:30:59.627 --> 00:31:02.876
the husband of the postmistress.
My father and me,

160
00:31:02.877 --> 00:31:05.501
we caught them in that Jewish woman's apartment,
on the fifth floor.

161
00:31:05.502 --> 00:31:08.501
They wanted to clear everything out.
You ought to have it confiscated.

162
00:31:08.502 --> 00:31:11.001
You did it yourself, you creep.
You and your father.

163
00:31:11.002 --> 00:31:13.543
Let's go.
Let's talk to the woman.

164
00:31:14.335 --> 00:31:16.460
She isn't upstairs.

165
00:31:32.793 --> 00:31:35.584
- Herr Fromm...
- For you I am still "Your Honour".

166
00:31:35.585 --> 00:31:40.126
- Who is your commanding officer?
- Escherich. Inspector Escherich.

167
00:31:40.127 --> 00:31:41.876
Police Headquarters, Prinz Albrecht Strasse.

168
00:31:41.877 --> 00:31:43.627
I know the address.

169
00:31:44.627 --> 00:31:48.460
Get him here.
And then you leave this apartment.

170
00:31:49.710 --> 00:31:52.668
Like hell I will.

171
00:31:53.085 --> 00:31:55.418
So, do you live alone?

172
00:31:58.793 --> 00:32:01.460
You don't mind if I look around, do you?

173
00:32:35.918 --> 00:32:37.502
Good day.

174
00:32:58.710 --> 00:33:02.418
You should have seen it.
Papa got into them, he had them scared.

175
00:33:03.335 --> 00:33:07.126
Then me and my brother went after him and
his buddy and really had them running.

176
00:33:07.127 --> 00:33:10.542
- Baldur?
- My brother's an SS Sturmbannfuhrer.

177
00:33:10.543 --> 00:33:13.377
Is that you?
Baldur Persicke?

178
00:33:14.752 --> 00:33:18.002
You often played in my apartment.

179
00:33:18.543 --> 00:33:22.877
You'd ring the bell, because I gave you apple cake.

180
00:33:25.168 --> 00:33:29.210
Right? How big you are now.

181
00:33:32.918 --> 00:33:35.002
And how strong.

182
00:33:46.585 --> 00:33:48.335
Get her out.

183
00:33:53.335 --> 00:33:55.042
- But...
- Just go!

184
00:33:55.043 --> 00:33:57.543
Heil Hitler!

185
00:34:01.752 --> 00:34:03.335
No!

186
00:35:47.793 --> 00:35:49.168
She is dead, Otto.

187
00:35:59.460 --> 00:36:01.168
I saw.

188
00:36:18.627 --> 00:36:22.084
You said you saw how Judge Fromm hid
the old woman at his place, didn't you?

189
00:36:22.085 --> 00:36:24.501
You know what's going on in this apartment house?

190
00:36:24.502 --> 00:36:28.792
A break-in, unlawful appropriation of national wealth,

191
00:36:28.793 --> 00:36:32.459
a denunciation of a respectable citizen.
Enough!

192
00:36:32.460 --> 00:36:33.792
Oh, I just...

193
00:36:33.793 --> 00:36:38.251
And a dead woman who was
very much alive a moment ago.

194
00:36:38.252 --> 00:36:40.584
You are not getting out of this one.

195
00:36:40.585 --> 00:36:43.209
You can't do this... No, you can't.

196
00:36:43.210 --> 00:36:45.459
Oh, yes, he can. But, he won't...

197
00:36:45.460 --> 00:36:47.917
because he's a police counselor and not a monster.

198
00:36:47.918 --> 00:36:51.876
I'm sure this gentleman didn't take
anything that doesn't belong to him.

199
00:36:51.877 --> 00:36:54.209
Because he knows exactly what that would mean.

200
00:36:54.210 --> 00:36:58.417
So, he will do what he does best
when he leaves this place.

201
00:36:58.418 --> 00:37:00.792
He will return to his comfortable little apartment.

202
00:37:00.793 --> 00:37:02.959
And he will observe what is going on here.

203
00:37:02.960 --> 00:37:05.960
- Yes, of course, Inspector. I will.
- You can leave now.

204
00:37:58.585 --> 00:38:00.959
Your Honour...
Did something happen?

205
00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:02.667
I mean, has Frau Rosenthal been...

206
00:38:02.668 --> 00:38:04.959
I don't know what you are talking about, Frau Kluge.

207
00:38:04.960 --> 00:38:07.460
Now, if you'll please excuse me?

208
00:39:48.335 --> 00:39:50.792
- I'll take these five cards, please.
- With stamps?

209
00:39:50.793 --> 00:39:54.377
No. I... I already have stamps.
Thank you.

210
00:39:54.918 --> 00:39:58.460
That makes twenty-five pfennig.
I'll wrap it up for you right away.

211
00:40:07.627 --> 00:40:10.376
I need gloves. Thin gloves.

212
00:40:10.377 --> 00:40:14.377
Sorry, we don't have any.
You might find some...

213
00:40:15.168 --> 00:40:19.085
- Let me think. Maybe you'll find them...
- No. It... it's fine. Just these.

214
00:40:20.210 --> 00:40:21.877
Thank you.

215
00:40:27.002 --> 00:40:29.043
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

216
00:40:29.877 --> 00:40:31.835
Good bye.

217
00:40:55.918 --> 00:40:58.960
STOP THE WAR MACHINE

218
00:41:07.085 --> 00:41:11.417
Listen... Hitler's shadow falls over
Europe like the devil's shadow.

219
00:41:11.418 --> 00:41:15.292
Pass this card on:
Down with the Hitler regime!

220
00:41:15.293 --> 00:41:18.751
What a scrawl!
Even my daughter writes better than that.

221
00:41:18.752 --> 00:41:20.209
Oh, yes?

222
00:41:20.210 --> 00:41:23.167
If you ask me, he is an incredibly stupid person.

223
00:41:23.168 --> 00:41:26.459
Someone from the lower classes
who works with their hands.

224
00:41:26.460 --> 00:41:29.459
Perhaps unskilled.
But stupid? No.

225
00:41:29.460 --> 00:41:33.043
Probably someone just letting off steam.
Just a flash in the pan.

226
00:41:37.918 --> 00:41:39.627
There is more?

227
00:41:41.252 --> 00:41:43.251
<i>“Mother.
The fuhrer murdered my son.</i>

228
00:41:43.252 --> 00:41:46.293
"Mother.
The Fuhrer will murder your sons, too."

229
00:41:47.168 --> 00:41:49.626
- Where?
- Neue Konigstrasse.

230
00:41:49.627 --> 00:41:52.334
Two weeks ago.
Another office building.

231
00:41:52.335 --> 00:41:53.460
Filth!

232
00:41:54.668 --> 00:41:57.085
So what do we do now?
Report it?

233
00:41:57.377 --> 00:42:00.918
If we had more men, it wouldn't be a problem.
We would catch this, er...

234
00:42:01.627 --> 00:42:06.585
How shall we call him?
Hobgoblin... in no time.

235
00:42:14.127 --> 00:42:15.876
I'd investigate everyone in Berlin

236
00:42:15.877 --> 00:42:18.292
...who has lost a son within the last two weeks.

237
00:42:18.293 --> 00:42:21.251
<i>- Why'?
- The fuhrer murdered my son.</i>

238
00:42:21.252 --> 00:42:24.167
- There's only one son.
- And?

239
00:42:24.168 --> 00:42:27.667
We wait. We collect information.
Put it together.

240
00:42:27.668 --> 00:42:31.335
That is our job. We are German professionals.
Not amateurs.

241
00:42:31.752 --> 00:42:35.377
What if he goes on doing it,
and no more cards are turned in?

242
00:42:35.668 --> 00:42:37.709
Who knows how long this has been going on.

243
00:42:37.710 --> 00:42:40.626
Think what it would be like to touch one
of these cards in a public place.

244
00:42:40.627 --> 00:42:43.084
To stand there, to read it,

245
00:42:43.085 --> 00:42:46.751
knowing somebody might be watching,
waiting to record your response.

246
00:42:46.752 --> 00:42:48.042
No.

247
00:42:48.043 --> 00:42:52.001
Whatever our Hobgoblin writes,
it's going to end up here with us.

248
00:42:52.002 --> 00:42:56.335
- Let's say... ninety-five percent.
- I say it's less.

249
00:42:58.460 --> 00:43:00.502
It's a bet?

250
00:43:05.793 --> 00:43:07.627
So, we wait.

251
00:43:08.043 --> 00:43:11.418
We wait for our friend to make a mistake.

252
00:44:11.127 --> 00:44:16.335
HITLERISM MEANS THAT MIGHT GOES
BEFORE RIGHT IN THE WORLD

253
00:44:33.377 --> 00:44:37.460
Quangel...

254
00:44:48.085 --> 00:44:49.460
Good morning.

255
00:45:03.835 --> 00:45:06.627
- Please come in.
- Thank you.

256
00:45:23.335 --> 00:45:25.334
- Heil Hitler!
- Heil Hitler!

257
00:45:25.335 --> 00:45:28.584
So, you're from the Nazi Women's League, my dear Frau...

258
00:45:28.585 --> 00:45:30.918
I'll just have the girl bring me my purse.

259
00:45:31.377 --> 00:45:34.417
I'm not here for a donation,
Frau Gehrich. Definitely not.

260
00:45:34.418 --> 00:45:36.751
So, what exactly can I do for you?

261
00:45:36.752 --> 00:45:40.626
Why aren't you at work?
Didn't you read our arms industry's calls for help?

262
00:45:40.627 --> 00:45:45.085
Look at me.
Do I look as if I'm suited to manual labour?

263
00:45:45.585 --> 00:45:47.418
Have you ever tried?

264
00:45:48.418 --> 00:45:51.377
I'm not about to jeopardise my health.

265
00:45:51.710 --> 00:45:54.042
Anyway, I can always get a medical certificate.

266
00:45:54.043 --> 00:45:56.792
Of course you can. You can buy one for
20 marks from your personal physician.

267
00:45:56.793 --> 00:45:58.459
But that won't help you in this case.

268
00:45:58.460 --> 00:46:00.209
In this case you'll need a doctor from a factory

269
00:46:00.210 --> 00:46:03.251
...to certify that you are unable to work.
A doctor that we assign to you.

270
00:46:03.252 --> 00:46:06.959
Alright. Assign me a doctor and you'll see what happens.

271
00:46:06.960 --> 00:46:08.834
You're mocking me and the Women's League?

272
00:46:08.835 --> 00:46:11.584
Making fun of our regulations and our Fuhrer?

273
00:46:11.585 --> 00:46:13.751
- I warn you.
- And I warn you.

274
00:46:13.752 --> 00:46:17.709
You don't seem to know who I am!
My husband is Obersturnnbamfuhrer!

275
00:46:17.710 --> 00:46:20.293
That makes it even worse, Frau Obersturmbannfuhrer.

276
00:46:21.210 --> 00:46:27.001
You'll hear from us.
Unless you have any more significant information?

277
00:46:27.002 --> 00:46:31.376
- An ill mother, perhaps?
- Your ID and your name. At once!

278
00:46:31.377 --> 00:46:33.167
I promise you, there will be consequences...

279
00:46:33.168 --> 00:46:39.543
Here you are. I don't have any calling cards because
I'm just a common worker.

280
00:46:41.127 --> 00:46:42.502
Heil Hitler!

281
00:46:54.835 --> 00:46:56.334
No, I don't understand.

282
00:46:56.335 --> 00:46:59.209
That woman comes under the Labour Service Duty Law.

283
00:46:59.210 --> 00:47:00.709
And you know that as well as I do.

284
00:47:00.710 --> 00:47:03.417
Frau Gehrich is the wife of an Obersturmbannfuhrer.

285
00:47:03.418 --> 00:47:04.834
So, I'm sure you understand that...

286
00:47:04.835 --> 00:47:08.959
Well, where does it say that women like
that are exempt from general duties?

287
00:47:08.960 --> 00:47:10.626
Where?
Don't be so obstinate!

288
00:47:10.627 --> 00:47:13.501
She has to look after her overworked husband.

289
00:47:13.502 --> 00:47:14.876
I do, too!

290
00:47:14.877 --> 00:47:19.417
And from what I saw, that woman has domestic help.

291
00:47:19.418 --> 00:47:23.042
I didn't do anything wrong.
I acted according to our regulations.

292
00:47:23.043 --> 00:47:26.834
So, are you going to apologise, Frau Quangel?

293
00:47:26.835 --> 00:47:31.918
- What for?
- Then I will do it, on your behalf.

294
00:47:32.377 --> 00:47:34.876
And you, you take some time off.

295
00:47:34.877 --> 00:47:37.709
Oh, you're throwing me out?
Because I told a woman like that the truth?

296
00:47:37.710 --> 00:47:40.751
- No, it's not...
- No, no. You misunderstood me.

297
00:47:40.752 --> 00:47:46.459
Just take some time off, and rest.
Gather your strength.

298
00:47:46.460 --> 00:47:50.418
- That's important, Anna.
- At a time of mourning.

299
00:47:51.710 --> 00:47:53.252
Alright?

300
00:47:56.210 --> 00:47:57.627
Alright.

301
00:48:00.418 --> 00:48:04.002
- Heil Hitler!
- Heil Hitler, Herr Quangel!

302
00:48:05.127 --> 00:48:07.252
And all the best for you, Anna.

303
00:48:17.377 --> 00:48:20.459
Thank God. No more Women's League.

304
00:48:20.460 --> 00:48:23.917
- Well done.
- How can you be so calm?

305
00:48:23.918 --> 00:48:26.501
I nearly died when I saw the gloves.

306
00:48:26.502 --> 00:48:29.292
Gloves, Anna. Just gloves.

307
00:48:29.293 --> 00:48:32.292
What are we doing, Otto?
We've lost our son.

308
00:48:32.293 --> 00:48:35.001
Other people have lost...

309
00:48:35.002 --> 00:48:37.252
But they, they don't...

310
00:48:39.293 --> 00:48:45.168
This system, this regime.
Now I feel that we're free.

311
00:48:45.460 --> 00:48:49.252
I mean, freed from all of it.

312
00:48:50.627 --> 00:48:52.877
This is how I feel.

313
00:49:14.918 --> 00:49:19.168
NO PEACE WITH HITLER'S DEVILISH
GOVERNMENT

314
00:49:24.502 --> 00:49:28.127
PASS THE FREE PRESS

315
00:49:31.002 --> 00:49:35.502
BELIEVE IN YOURSELF,
NOT IN HITLER'S GANG

316
00:49:39.210 --> 00:49:42.793
HITLERISM MEANS A WORLD OF VIOLENCE
AND INJUSTICE

317
00:49:43.335 --> 00:49:46.960
IT WILL NEVER BRING PEACE.

318
00:49:59.835 --> 00:50:02.418
Luderitzstrasse twenty-three.

319
00:50:14.960 --> 00:50:18.377
- Next.
- Amsterdamer strasse twenty-seven.

320
00:51:23.627 --> 00:51:25.084
Hey, Quangel!

321
00:51:25.085 --> 00:51:27.167
Where are you going?
Get into the shelter!

322
00:51:27.168 --> 00:51:31.460
It's a shelter for mothers and children, boy.
So it's not suitable for us.

323
00:52:05.335 --> 00:52:07.876
What are you doing here?
What are you doing?

324
00:52:07.877 --> 00:52:09.918
Stop! What...

325
00:52:11.127 --> 00:52:14.043
Hey, you! Stop!

326
00:52:16.460 --> 00:52:20.585
Wait! Stop! Stop!

327
00:52:23.377 --> 00:52:25.252
Wait!

328
00:52:31.502 --> 00:52:32.793
Stop!

329
00:52:56.627 --> 00:52:58.960
Hey, you! Wait!

330
00:52:59.585 --> 00:53:01.543
Who are you?

331
00:53:02.502 --> 00:53:05.834
Please, can you help me?
I need to find the shelter for mothers and children.

332
00:53:05.835 --> 00:53:08.251
I've lost my way.
My daughter is waiting for me there.

333
00:53:08.252 --> 00:53:10.667
You must know your way around here.
Please.

334
00:53:10.668 --> 00:53:12.667
Your daughter, you say?
How old is she?

335
00:53:12.668 --> 00:53:15.959
She's only six years old!
Waiting for me at the shelter, she said...

336
00:53:15.960 --> 00:53:18.917
- and now there and I am not.
- Ya, two blocks and you're there.

337
00:53:18.918 --> 00:53:20.376
Yes, calm now, calm down.

338
00:53:20.377 --> 00:53:22.459
The people there will take care of her.

339
00:53:22.460 --> 00:53:26.251
I'm sure she's frightened and crying...
It's two blocks, you say?

340
00:53:26.252 --> 00:53:29.460
Yes, two blocks, and then left.
You can't miss it.

341
00:53:52.293 --> 00:53:56.585
- Heil Hitler!
- Heil Hitler!

342
00:53:59.335 --> 00:54:02.542
Well, Inspector,
let's see what your filthy hack is up to.

343
00:54:02.543 --> 00:54:05.334
I hear he's still scribbling away,
right under your nose, huh?

344
00:54:05.335 --> 00:54:07.418
Heil Hitler, Standartenfuhrer.

345
00:54:08.585 --> 00:54:12.251
He won't give up.
It wasn't to be expected anyway.

346
00:54:12.252 --> 00:54:17.126
Someone who takes one and a half hours
to draw that is persistent.

347
00:54:17.127 --> 00:54:18.667
- Tried it myself.
- Oh, really?

348
00:54:18.668 --> 00:54:22.167
But rest assured: I always find my man.

349
00:54:22.168 --> 00:54:24.167
We run our Operation Hobgoblin... around the clock.

350
00:54:24.168 --> 00:54:26.752
- Hobgoblin?
- Yes.

351
00:54:27.085 --> 00:54:30.002
- I like that.
- Glad to hear that.

352
00:54:31.043 --> 00:54:35.167
Judging by the distribution,
the man lives somewhere around Alexander Square.

353
00:54:35.168 --> 00:54:37.292
There were no cards here at first.

354
00:54:37.293 --> 00:54:39.001
But now he doesn't want to travel so far

355
00:54:39.002 --> 00:54:41.918
...and leaves more and more cards in his own neighbourhood.

356
00:54:42.585 --> 00:54:45.543
- Heil Hitler, Standartenfuhrer.
- How many?

357
00:54:47.085 --> 00:54:50.709
He also includes the eastern districts... and downtown.

358
00:54:50.710 --> 00:54:52.543
Here, look.

359
00:54:53.543 --> 00:54:57.709
I asked you a question, Escherich.
How many?

360
00:54:57.710 --> 00:55:00.251
One hundred and twenty-seven, Standartenfuhrer.

361
00:55:00.252 --> 00:55:04.709
One hundred and twenty-nine, to be exact,
with these two from this morning.

362
00:55:04.710 --> 00:55:07.752
- More than a hundred!
- Yes.

363
00:55:08.127 --> 00:55:10.709
If more than a hundred cards were turned in here,

364
00:55:10.710 --> 00:55:14.751
doesn't anyone of you wise asses
ever think about how much filth

365
00:55:14.752 --> 00:55:16.792
...is still circulating out there?

366
00:55:16.793 --> 00:55:19.626
With due respect, let's think about human nature.

367
00:55:19.627 --> 00:55:22.334
No one holds onto these scribblings
longer than necessary...

368
00:55:22.335 --> 00:55:26.501
Tell me who's been doing this, because I will be asked,

369
00:55:26.502 --> 00:55:28.585
and I have to answer.

370
00:55:29.502 --> 00:55:30.877
Now.

371
00:55:32.752 --> 00:55:35.418
"The Heroic battle of Stalingrad."

372
00:55:37.377 --> 00:55:40.085
Someone has to write the truth.

373
00:55:40.377 --> 00:55:42.002
With all these lies.

374
00:55:47.835 --> 00:55:50.168
What do you think happens to our cards?

375
00:55:51.043 --> 00:55:53.293
Why do you want to know?

376
00:55:56.085 --> 00:56:00.710
- I want to know how people react.
- Some people will be afraid, probably.

377
00:56:01.127 --> 00:56:04.502
Afraid that someone
may have watched them pick up the card.

378
00:56:05.793 --> 00:56:09.210
Some will maybe put them back.

379
00:56:09.460 --> 00:56:14.418
Some people will turn them in to policemen,
block wardens...

380
00:56:14.960 --> 00:56:18.251
But our cards will also be read by them...

381
00:56:18.252 --> 00:56:20.293
It's like... with a machine.

382
00:56:22.002 --> 00:56:25.752
A little sand in the gears will not stop the machine.

383
00:56:27.377 --> 00:56:31.376
But if a person throws a little more sand, and...

384
00:56:31.377 --> 00:56:35.918
and more the motor begins

385
00:56:36.793 --> 00:56:39.127
...to the assembly line stops.

386
00:56:40.335 --> 00:56:45.252
In stutter... my mind I see lots of people
throwing sand in the gears.

387
00:56:46.877 --> 00:56:48.877
You are a romantic, Otto Quangel.

388
00:56:51.127 --> 00:56:54.877
I'm a mechanic.

389
00:56:58.043 --> 00:57:00.335
You are the romantic.

390
00:57:00.627 --> 00:57:04.959
- At least, you used to be.
- What? I used to be?

391
00:57:04.960 --> 00:57:09.793
Still, I saw you first. Not the other way around.

392
00:57:10.460 --> 00:57:12.377
But you didn't say anything.

393
00:57:13.418 --> 00:57:16.335
You were dancing with Peter Reinke.

394
00:57:16.793 --> 00:57:19.501
And then you went with him to the chestnut tree.

395
00:57:19.502 --> 00:57:22.126
You with your crown of flowers.

396
00:57:22.127 --> 00:57:25.251
Laughing, as if he was incredibly funny.

397
00:57:25.252 --> 00:57:28.710
Reinke... with his stupid haircut.

398
00:57:29.377 --> 00:57:32.126
He's bald now and a member of the Party.

399
00:57:32.127 --> 00:57:36.918
I would have danced with you, too, but you didn't ask.

400
00:57:38.252 --> 00:57:40.543
You knew the way I looked at you.

401
00:57:41.252 --> 00:57:43.793
Anyway, I asked you two years later.

402
00:57:44.168 --> 00:57:46.502
Not to dance.

403
00:58:17.460 --> 00:58:19.668
So, you'd like a dance?

404
00:58:22.377 --> 00:58:24.918
No. Just".

405
00:58:45.585 --> 00:58:49.126
- Is that him? Approximately?
- Yes, pretty much.

406
00:58:49.127 --> 00:58:53.084
His eyes might be a little bit further apart.
It was dark...

407
00:58:53.085 --> 00:58:55.876
Thank you. You've done the Reich a great service.

408
00:58:55.877 --> 00:58:57.835
Heil Hitler, Inspector.

409
00:58:58.793 --> 00:59:00.835
Fraulein Schaefer.

410
00:59:02.168 --> 00:59:03.793
Have this passed around.

411
00:59:43.918 --> 00:59:47.792
"Pass the information.
Join the free press."

412
00:59:47.793 --> 00:59:53.293
"Fear has taken control of you.
Kill it. Kill Hitler."

413
00:59:54.752 --> 00:59:58.542
It's a man who is no longer young, who
lost his only son in the French Campaign.

414
00:59:58.543 --> 01:00:00.876
Inexperienced at writing, but intelligent.

415
01:00:00.877 --> 01:00:03.501
The style has visibly changed
during the course of the year.

416
01:00:03.502 --> 01:00:05.209
HITLER MURDERER

417
01:00:05.210 --> 01:00:07.960
In recent months he has used the title "Free Press".

418
01:00:08.627 --> 01:00:11.376
He's working in an increasingly professional way.

419
01:00:11.377 --> 01:00:14.126
He never leaves fingerprints.
He operates strategically.

420
01:00:14.127 --> 01:00:17.584
He never chooses the same street twice in a row.

421
01:00:17.585 --> 01:00:23.793
He always changes between these streetcar lines:
seven, nine and eleven.

422
01:00:42.627 --> 01:00:46.042
"Each thought against the National Socialists"

423
01:00:46.043 --> 01:00:50.043
"is like sand in the criminal war machine."

424
01:00:53.668 --> 01:00:56.502
"Pass on this card.
Free Press!"

425
01:01:00.252 --> 01:01:02.752
"How many children have to die?"

426
01:01:03.460 --> 01:01:07.335
"Fear is their only weapon...
Free Press!"

427
01:01:07.627 --> 01:01:11.085
"Help us to put an end
to the criminal war machine."

428
01:01:11.502 --> 01:01:16.085
Zott. Again and again the picture of a machine.

429
01:01:19.543 --> 01:01:21.043
Papers?

430
01:01:23.377 --> 01:01:25.335
Papers.

431
01:02:50.793 --> 01:02:53.252
Today is the twenty-second.

432
01:02:57.335 --> 01:02:59.710
- Today.
- Birthday.

433
01:03:14.377 --> 01:03:15.835
Come.

434
01:03:38.168 --> 01:03:42.377
Sometimes I feel the danger as if it were so physical.

435
01:03:43.502 --> 01:03:47.293
- I actually feel it.
- Please. Don't frighten me.

436
01:03:49.335 --> 01:03:50.793
No.

437
01:04:02.127 --> 01:04:04.252
- To Hans.
- Hans.

438
01:04:15.960 --> 01:04:19.043
No. Inspector Escherich isn't in his office.
Just a moment.

439
01:04:20.835 --> 01:04:22.334
Operator speaking.

440
01:04:22.335 --> 01:04:24.417
Incoming call from the Lothringer Street Section.

441
01:04:24.418 --> 01:04:27.459
Reported arrest of suspect in the Hobgoblin case.

442
01:04:27.460 --> 01:04:28.793
Yes, I'll put you through.

443
01:04:51.918 --> 01:04:54.543
- Anna!
- Oh, hello, Walter.

444
01:04:55.002 --> 01:04:56.917
Did he run away? Poor girl.

445
01:04:56.918 --> 01:05:00.334
No. I just brought him his lunch box.
He left it again.

446
01:05:00.335 --> 01:05:03.918
Oh, I thought he was ill. He isn't here.

447
01:05:32.877 --> 01:05:35.876
Anna! How are you doing? You look great.

448
01:05:35.877 --> 01:05:38.043
I'm getting married soon!

449
01:05:58.710 --> 01:06:02.127
- What are you doing here?
- We said we would do this together.

450
01:06:05.085 --> 01:06:07.210
- Why didn't you go to work?
- Not now.

451
01:06:21.460 --> 01:06:24.377
Do you know what my day was like?

452
01:06:25.960 --> 01:06:27.751
No. You don't think of that, do you?

453
01:06:27.752 --> 01:06:29.417
Finding you're not at work and then thinking

454
01:06:29.418 --> 01:06:32.042
you are still inside that building.
You know what that's like for me?

455
01:06:32.043 --> 01:06:34.752
What is it, Otto? You want to get caught?
Is that what it is?

456
01:06:43.252 --> 01:06:45.917
- Nothing happened.
- Nothing happened?

457
01:06:45.918 --> 01:06:48.209
Did you see who they arrested?

458
01:06:48.210 --> 01:06:51.334
A bum. He probably stole something.
It has nothing to do with us.

459
01:06:51.335 --> 01:06:55.334
That's the husband of our postmistress!

460
01:06:55.335 --> 01:06:57.834
What makes you think it has nothing to do with us?

461
01:06:57.835 --> 01:06:59.627
They're divorced.

462
01:07:00.502 --> 01:07:03.792
That doesn't mean anything, damn it!

463
01:07:03.793 --> 01:07:08.667
I was so afraid for you. What if it's a... a sign?

464
01:07:08.668 --> 01:07:12.252
- If it's a warning?
- It isn't.

465
01:07:14.752 --> 01:07:16.168
Stay calm.

466
01:07:22.793 --> 01:07:25.251
Remember, when Hans died,

467
01:07:25.252 --> 01:07:28.627
you said your life wasn't worth a thing?

468
01:07:31.127 --> 01:07:33.292
You were right.

469
01:07:33.293 --> 01:07:37.126
That's why we can be free.
Why we don't have to be afraid.

470
01:07:37.127 --> 01:07:42.460
But your life.
Otto, your life means something to me now.

471
01:07:42.960 --> 01:07:46.627
Means... Means... everything to me now.

472
01:07:50.543 --> 01:07:53.709
We said we'd do this together.

473
01:07:53.710 --> 01:07:57.127
- We won't stop.
- Aren't you afraid?

474
01:08:01.502 --> 01:08:03.334
Today I stayed again to watch.

475
01:08:03.335 --> 01:08:06.793
I need to see what happens when people read it.

476
01:08:30.752 --> 01:08:32.668
Come... come.

477
01:08:39.127 --> 01:08:41.542
My sick certificate had expired.

478
01:08:41.543 --> 01:08:43.709
That's why I went to see the doctor.

479
01:08:43.710 --> 01:08:47.793
They'll send me to a camp otherwise.
Please. I swear.

480
01:08:48.043 --> 01:08:51.792
By the lives of my children. Please.

481
01:08:51.793 --> 01:08:54.835
Two sons? And they're both soldiers, right?

482
01:08:55.085 --> 01:08:57.834
Both of them. Yes.

483
01:08:57.835 --> 01:09:01.167
One of them is even in the Waffen-SS.

484
01:09:01.168 --> 01:09:05.127
- And they're both alive, I hope?
- Yes. Here.

485
01:09:05.710 --> 01:09:08.377
Our Karl. In Poland.

486
01:09:13.418 --> 01:09:17.626
Well, that's good news.

487
01:09:17.627 --> 01:09:19.876
So, the man was caught red handed.
There are witnesses.

488
01:09:19.877 --> 01:09:23.001
And here... the corpus delicti.
It's obviously the writing of our Hobgoblin.

489
01:09:23.002 --> 01:09:24.626
Come on, we've got him!

490
01:09:24.627 --> 01:09:27.376
You know the criminal's profile as well as I do, Zott.

491
01:09:27.377 --> 01:09:30.167
We're looking for a mechanic who lost his only son.

492
01:09:30.168 --> 01:09:32.751
And then you drag in this ridiculous character.

493
01:09:32.752 --> 01:09:36.626
A gambler. Who doesn't even live near our target area.

494
01:09:36.627 --> 01:09:39.502
With two children who are very much alive.

495
01:09:39.877 --> 01:09:42.959
Does that...
Does that mean you believe me, Inspector?

496
01:09:42.960 --> 01:09:46.585
- Yes. You can go.
- Thank you. God bless you.

497
01:09:51.918 --> 01:09:52.918
Bravo.

498
01:09:56.293 --> 01:09:58.084
You did what?

499
01:09:58.085 --> 01:10:01.667
- You let your Hobbygobby go?
- Hobgoblin, Standartenfuhrer.

500
01:10:01.668 --> 01:10:04.667
With due respect, you may be my superior,

501
01:10:04.668 --> 01:10:09.167
but as a member of the SS
you are not necessarily a criminalist.

502
01:10:09.168 --> 01:10:12.751
I'm a policeman. And I'm asking you to let me do my job,

503
01:10:12.752 --> 01:10:15.002
just as I have learned from my experience...

504
01:10:15.793 --> 01:10:17.502
<i>Experience?</i>

505
01:10:19.377 --> 01:10:22.292
I know all about guys like you!
Intellectuals.

506
01:10:22.293 --> 01:10:25.835
Wise guys!
Don't mess up my floor!

507
01:10:26.002 --> 01:10:28.418
Swallow your damned blood!

508
01:10:28.668 --> 01:10:32.084
Up! Up, up, up!

509
01:10:32.085 --> 01:10:34.585
Come. UP!

510
01:10:36.543 --> 01:10:37.751
You think you're clever?

511
01:10:37.752 --> 01:10:41.417
And we're just the guys from the SS
who don't have a clue, right?

512
01:10:41.418 --> 01:10:44.377
Say it. I want to hear it.
I'm smarter than you guys.

513
01:10:44.710 --> 01:10:46.002
Say it!

514
01:10:46.335 --> 01:10:50.043
- Say it! I can't hear you!
- I'm sorry.

515
01:10:53.210 --> 01:10:55.043
You have two days...

516
01:10:56.085 --> 01:10:59.084
Two days to eliminate the guy you let go.

517
01:10:59.085 --> 01:11:01.335
Now get rid of that thing!

518
01:12:21.418 --> 01:12:25.460
Frau Quangel? You're Hans's mother, right?

519
01:12:26.043 --> 01:12:28.252
- Yes.
- Dietrich.

520
01:12:28.460 --> 01:12:32.627
- I was one of Hans's classmates.
- Dietrich... Of course.

521
01:12:33.002 --> 01:12:35.834
- How are you?
- Fine, thank you.

522
01:12:35.835 --> 01:12:40.293
- Well, I'm... alive.
- I'm glad you've come back.

523
01:12:42.252 --> 01:12:45.835
- Herr Necker?
- Excuse me, I have to go.

524
01:12:48.960 --> 01:12:53.460
You know, Frau Quangel, I...
I miss Hans a lot.

525
01:13:19.918 --> 01:13:22.752
I have nothing to do with Enno anymore.

526
01:13:24.127 --> 01:13:26.918
He hasn't been my husband for a long time.

527
01:13:27.627 --> 01:13:29.252
Before God.

528
01:13:36.377 --> 01:13:38.127
Now...

529
01:13:38.543 --> 01:13:40.752
where were we? Ah, yes.

530
01:13:41.418 --> 01:13:45.210
You were about to tell me
how to find that ex-husband of yours.

531
01:14:08.918 --> 01:14:11.043
So, here you've been hiding?

532
01:14:13.543 --> 01:14:15.709
I know you've nothing to do with the cards, Enno.

533
01:14:15.710 --> 01:14:16.959
That's good news, Inspector...

534
01:14:16.960 --> 01:14:19.585
But the guys from the SS think it was you.

535
01:14:20.460 --> 01:14:22.918
And I'm afraid they're in charge now.

536
01:14:25.543 --> 01:14:27.293
In charge of me, too.

537
01:14:28.960 --> 01:14:32.127
They will arrest you.
They will interrogate you.

538
01:14:32.502 --> 01:14:34.502
In their own way.

539
01:14:37.252 --> 01:14:39.710
I'd rather be dead...

540
01:14:41.585 --> 01:14:43.210
You're right.

541
01:14:44.252 --> 01:14:46.168
You'd rather be dead.

542
01:15:06.043 --> 01:15:07.793
It's alright.

543
01:15:08.210 --> 01:15:09.835
It's better this way.

544
01:15:12.418 --> 01:15:13.960
No, please, no!

545
01:15:29.793 --> 01:15:34.668
Suicide?
Good news, Escherich.

546
01:15:36.293 --> 01:15:38.252
The noose has tightened.

547
01:15:41.377 --> 01:15:45.793
- No new cards?
- Not yet. No.

548
01:17:50.877 --> 01:17:53.293
Thanks for taking over for Fritz.

549
01:18:02.918 --> 01:18:04.460
It's getting closer.

550
01:18:31.918 --> 01:18:35.501
Foreman Quangel.
A machine is overheating.

551
01:18:35.502 --> 01:18:37.418
Turn it off!

552
01:19:57.710 --> 01:19:59.710
Don't you have anything to do?

553
01:20:13.168 --> 01:20:15.085
Ludwig!

554
01:20:17.085 --> 01:20:19.460
There's something for you.

555
01:20:27.835 --> 01:20:31.085
It's quite something!
You'd better take it to the management.

556
01:20:31.793 --> 01:20:35.960
You're a Party representative. You have to do it.

557
01:20:36.585 --> 01:20:38.710
Stick by the rules.

558
01:20:57.918 --> 01:20:59.210
Yes?

559
01:21:13.918 --> 01:21:16.667
Everyone on today's shift?
Their names? Addresses?

560
01:21:16.668 --> 01:21:18.126
Of course.

561
01:21:18.127 --> 01:21:20.501
Our man must live somewhere between Christburger,

562
01:21:20.502 --> 01:21:25.127
- Chodowiecki and Jablonskistrasse.
- No, nobody with that address, Inspector.

563
01:21:26.918 --> 01:21:29.167
Who is the foreman?
Who knows his men best?

564
01:21:29.168 --> 01:21:31.292
- That's Fritz Kéimper.
- Get him here at once.

565
01:21:31.293 --> 01:21:32.626
That's impossible.

566
01:21:32.627 --> 01:21:35.584
- He injured himself this morning.
- And who replaced him?

567
01:21:35.585 --> 01:21:38.126
Otto Quangel. From the other shift.

568
01:21:38.127 --> 01:21:40.667
His name is not on the list.
I thought it was complete.

569
01:21:40.668 --> 01:21:43.251
Sorry. He's just helping out today.

570
01:21:43.252 --> 01:21:46.460
- Of course, he does not know the people.
- Where does he live?

571
01:21:47.377 --> 01:21:49.543
Otto Quangel?

572
01:22:05.710 --> 01:22:07.293
Walter, where is Otto?

573
01:22:48.210 --> 01:22:52.960
- Good morning, Foreman Quangel.
- Morning.

574
01:22:57.293 --> 01:22:59.627
Please, have a seat.

575
01:23:18.335 --> 01:23:20.210
Frau Quangel!

576
01:23:22.335 --> 01:23:24.252
We know you're here!

577
01:23:25.210 --> 01:23:27.043
Open the door!

578
01:23:46.460 --> 01:23:48.252
Look at this, Quangel.

579
01:23:49.293 --> 01:23:51.293
This will surely interest you.

580
01:23:52.793 --> 01:23:54.793
What do you think that is?

581
01:24:03.168 --> 01:24:05.252
Don't even make the effort, Quangel.

582
01:24:07.877 --> 01:24:12.043
There are exactly two-hundred and sixty-seven cards.

583
01:24:16.543 --> 01:24:18.293
Is that the number you were looking for?

584
01:24:19.335 --> 01:24:21.210
Think about it, Quangel.

585
01:24:21.877 --> 01:24:25.626
Every single card was voluntarily turned in to us.
Voluntarily.

586
01:24:25.627 --> 01:24:27.877
We didn't find any ourselves.

587
01:24:28.335 --> 01:24:31.293
They couldn't wait to hand them over to us,
all those people.

588
01:24:32.210 --> 01:24:35.627
Some were arrested.
One committed suicide.

589
01:24:38.168 --> 01:24:41.709
How could you seriously believe
that you would change anything?

590
01:24:41.710 --> 01:24:44.627
You, Foreman Quangel.

591
01:24:46.293 --> 01:24:48.126
- Who killed himself?
- It doesn't matter.

592
01:24:48.127 --> 01:24:52.752
- A small fish. Insignificant.
- Everyone is significant.

593
01:24:54.210 --> 01:24:57.502
- It's my fault.
- Oh, there we go.

594
01:24:57.918 --> 01:25:00.335
Now you have admitted your crime.

595
01:25:01.668 --> 01:25:05.793
Tell me, Quangel, precisely.
How many cards did you write yourself?

596
01:25:06.418 --> 01:25:08.377
I mean, altogether.

597
01:25:09.377 --> 01:25:11.502
Two-hundred and eighty-five.

598
01:25:13.418 --> 01:25:14.543
Eighteen.

599
01:25:17.752 --> 01:25:20.043
Eighteen cards weren't turned in.

600
01:25:23.918 --> 01:25:26.460
By the way. We have Anna.

601
01:25:28.835 --> 01:25:31.501
Then let her go.
She has nothing to do with it.

602
01:25:31.502 --> 01:25:35.334
I know you're lying, Quangel.
Your wife dictated what to write.

603
01:25:35.335 --> 01:25:38.335
Do I look like someone who would
let his wife dictate things to him?

604
01:25:40.210 --> 01:25:42.667
It was my idea from the beginning.

605
01:25:42.668 --> 01:25:46.542
I thought it all up. I carried it out by myself.

606
01:25:46.543 --> 01:25:49.418
- She confessed.
- Now you're lying.

607
01:25:50.543 --> 01:25:53.668
She confessed.
She didn't want you to get all the credit.

608
01:25:59.668 --> 01:26:01.418
I'll sign my confession.

609
01:26:02.793 --> 01:26:04.627
But, Inspector...

610
01:26:05.127 --> 01:26:08.668
Anna. Please... don't...

611
01:26:12.210 --> 01:26:16.210
It's... It's not necessary.

612
01:26:28.252 --> 01:26:30.460
Send a recording clerk to my office.

613
01:27:04.127 --> 01:27:05.960
Escherich.

614
01:27:21.043 --> 01:27:23.043
To the Hobgoblin!

615
01:27:59.960 --> 01:28:01.377
Quangel.

616
01:29:17.168 --> 01:29:19.877
- Anna.
- Otto.

617
01:29:39.502 --> 01:29:42.293
- You know what will happen?
- Yes.

618
01:29:44.085 --> 01:29:46.002
It can't be changed.

619
01:29:46.627 --> 01:29:48.960
I know, Otto.

620
01:29:52.335 --> 01:29:53.793
It doesn't matter.

621
01:29:56.918 --> 01:29:58.377
No.

622
01:30:16.168 --> 01:30:17.502
All rise!

623
01:30:27.752 --> 01:30:30.627
- Heil Hitler!
- Heil Hitler!

624
01:30:49.085 --> 01:30:50.835
Time's up!

625
01:31:01.335 --> 01:31:03.960
Don't be afraid, my child.

626
01:31:05.585 --> 01:31:07.377
Don't be afraid.

627
01:31:17.293 --> 01:31:21.584
Judge Fromm, would you stay with me a moment?

628
01:31:21.585 --> 01:31:24.335
I'll close my eyes and pretend it is Otto.

629
01:32:01.543 --> 01:32:03.043
Time, Quangel.

630
01:32:09.710 --> 01:32:11.543
Put these on.

631
01:32:39.043 --> 01:32:44.043
Can I do something for you?
Is there something you need?

632
01:32:44.502 --> 01:32:46.502
A card and a pen?

633
01:32:51.377 --> 01:32:53.668
You took her, anyway.

634
01:34:13.085 --> 01:34:15.627
I read all your cards, Hobgoblin.

635
01:34:16.752 --> 01:34:19.752
Yours and your wife's.

636
01:34:21.168 --> 01:34:24.960
I am the only person who read all of them.

637
01:34:26.668 --> 01:34:29.043
All of them except for eighteen.

638
01:34:32.252 --> 01:34:34.127
Eighteen cards.

639
01:35:50.502 --> 01:35:53.792
IN MEMORY OF OTTO AND ELISE HAMPEL

640
01:35:53.793 --> 01:35:57.334
GUILLOTINED FOR HAVING WRITTEN
AND CIRCULATED CARDS

641
01:35:57.335 --> 01:36:01.168
AGAINST THE NAZI REGIME
BETWEEN 1940 AND 1943.
